" (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/open-mmlab/mmdetection/v3.3.0/configs/rtmdet/rtmdet-ins_tiny_8xb32-300e_coco.py)\nciteturn239view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago; Content type: text/plain; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/open-mmlab/mmdetection/v3.3.0/configs/rtmdet/rtmdet-ins_tiny_8xb32-300e_coco.py\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 46\nL0: _base_ = './rtmdet-ins_s_8xb32-300e_coco.py'\nL1: \nL2: checkpoint = 'https://download.openmmlab.com/mmdetection/v3.0/rtmdet/cspnext_rsb_pretrain/cspnext-tiny_imagenet_600e.pth'  # noqa\nL3: \nL4: model = dict(\nL5:     backbone=dict(\nL6:         deepen_factor=0.167,\nL7:         widen_factor=0.375,\nL8:         init_cfg=dict(\nL9:             type='Pretrained', prefix='backbone.', checkpoint=checkpoint)),\nL10:     neck=dict(in_channels=[96, 192, 384], out_channels=96, num_csp_blocks=1),\nL11:     bbox_head=dict(in_channels=96, feat_channels=96))\nL12: train_pipeline = [\nL13:     dict(type='LoadImageFromFile', backend_args={{_base_.backend_args}}),\nL14:     dict(\nL15:         type='LoadAnnotations',\nL16:         with_bbox=True,\nL17:         with_mask=True,\nL18:         poly2mask=False),\nL19:     dict(\nL20:         type='CachedMosaic',\nL21:         img_scale=(640, 640),\nL22:         pad_val=114.0,\nL23:         max_cached_images=20,\nL24:         random_pop=False),\nL25:     dict(\nL26:         type='RandomResize',\nL27:         scale=(1280, 1280),\nL28:         ratio_range=(0.5, 2.0),\nL29:         keep_ratio=True),\nL30:     dict(type='RandomCrop', crop_size=(640, 640)),\nL31:     dict(type='YOLOXHSVRandomAug'),\nL32:     dict(type='RandomFlip', prob=0.5),\nL33:     dict(type='Pad', size=(640, 640), pad_val=dict(img=(114, 114, 114))),\nL34:     dict(\nL35:         type='CachedMixUp',\nL36:         img_scale=(640, 640),\nL37:         ratio_range=(1.0, 1.0),\nL38:         max_cached_images=10,\nL39:         random_pop=False,\nL40:         pad_val=(114, 114, 114),\nL41:         prob=0.5),\nL42:     dict(type='FilterAnnotations', min_gt_bbox_wh=(1, 1)),\nL43:     dict(type='PackDetInputs')\nL44: ]\nL45: train_dataloader = dict(dataset=dict(pipeline=train_pipeline))\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nraw.githubusercontent.com (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/open-mmlab/mmdetection/v3.3.0/configs/solov2/solov2-light_r18_fpn_ms-3x_coco.py)\nciteturn239view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; Content type: text/plain; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/open-mmlab/mmdetection/v3.3.0/configs/solov2/solov2-light_r18_fpn_ms-3x_coco.py\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: _base_ = './solov2-light_r50_fpn_ms-3x_coco.py' # model settings model = dict( backbone=dict( depth=18, init_cfg=dict(checkpoint='torchvision://resnet18')), neck=dict(in_channels=[64, 128, 256, 512]))\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInstallation — mmcv 2.2.0 documentation (https://mmcv.readthedocs.io/en/latest/get_started/installation.html)\nciteturn239view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://mmcv.readthedocs.io/en/latest/get_started/installation.html\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 129\nL0:   * cite0†GitHub†github.com L1:   * Docs\nL2: cite1†MMEngine†mmengine.readthedocs.io cite2†MMCV cite3†MMEval†mmeval.readthedocs.io cite4†MIM†openmim.readthedocs.io cite5†MMAction2†mmaction2.readthedocs.io cite6†MMPreTrain†mmpretrain.readthedocs.io cite7†MMDetection†mmdetection.readthedocs.io cite8†MMDetection3D†mmdetection3d.readthedocs.io cite9†MMagic†mmagic.readthedocs.io cite10†MMOCR†mmocr.readthedocs.io cite11†MMPose†mmpose.readthedocs.io cite12†MMSegmentation†mmsegmentation.readthedocs.io cite13†MMTracking†mmtracking.readthedocs.io cite14†MMFlow†mmflow.readthedocs.io cite15†MMFewShot†mmfewshot.readthedocs.io cite16†MMHuman3D†mmhuman3d.readthedocs.io cite17†MMRazor†mmrazor.readthedocs.io cite18†MMDeploy†mmdeploy.readthedocs.io cite19†MMRotate†mmrotate.readthedocs.io cite20†MMYOLO†mmyolo.readthedocs.io L3:   * OpenMMLab\nL4: \nL5: cite21†Homepage†openmmlab.com cite22†Open Platform†platform.openmmlab.com cite23†GitHub†github.com cite24†Twitter†twitter.com cite25†Zhihu†zhihu.com L6: \nL7: Table of Contents\nL8: \nL9: Shortcuts\nL10: # Installationcite26†¶ L11: \nL12: There are two versions of MMCV:\nL13: \nL14:   * mmcv: comprehensive, with full features and various CUDA ops out of box. It takes longer time to build.\nL15: \nL16:   * mmcv-lite: lite, without CUDA ops but all other features, similar to mmcv<1.0.0. It is useful when you do not need those CUDA ops.\nL17: \nL18: Warning\nL19: Do not install both versions in the same environment, otherwise you may encounter errors like `ModuleNotFound`. You need to uninstall one before installing the other. `Installing the full version is highly recommended if CUDA is avaliable`.\nL20: ## Install mmcvcite27†¶ L21: \nL22: Before installing mmcv, make sure that PyTorch has been successfully installed following the cite28†PyTorch official installation guide†pytorch.org . This can be verified using the following command\nL23: \nL24:     python -c 'import torch;print(torch.__version__)'\nL25: \nL26: \nL27: If version information is output, then PyTorch is installed.\nL28: ### Install with mim (recommended)cite29†¶ L29: \nL30: cite30†mim†github.com is the package management tool for the OpenMMLab projects, which makes it easy to install mmcv\nL31: \nL32:     pip install -U openmim\nL33:     mim install mmcv\nL34: \nL35: \nL36: If you find that the above installation command does not use a pre-built package ending with `.whl` but a source package ending with `.tar.gz`, you may not have a pre-build package corresponding to the PyTorch or CUDA or mmcv version, in which case you can cite31†build mmcv from source .\nL37: Installation log using pre-built packages\nL38: \nL39: Looking in links: https://download.openmmlab.com/mmcv/dist/cu102/torch1.8.0/index.html\nL40: Collecting mmcv\nL41: Downloading https://download.openmmlab.com/mmcv/dist/cu102/torch1.8.0/mmcv-2.0.0-cp38-cp38-manylinux1_x86_64.whl\nL42: \nL43: Installation log using source packages\nL44: \nL45: Looking in links: https://download.openmmlab.com/mmcv/dist/cu102/torch1.8.0/index.html\nL46: Collecting mmcv==2.0.0\nL47: Downloading mmcv-2.0.0.tar.gz\nL48: To install a specific version of mmcv, for example, mmcv version 2.0.0, you can use the following command\nL49: \nL50:     mim install mmcv==2.0.0\nL51: \nL52: \nL53: Note\nL54: \nL55: If you would like to use `opencv-python-headless` instead of `opencv-python`, e.g., in a minimum container environment or servers without GUI, you can first install it before installing MMCV to skip the installation of `opencv-python`.\nL56: Alternatively, if it takes too long to install a dependency library, you can specify the pypi source\nL57: \nL58:     mim install mmcv -i https://pypi.tuna.tsinghua.edu.cn/simple\nL59: \nL60: \nL61: You can run cite32†check_installation.py†github.com to check the installation of mmcv-full after running the installation commands.\nL62: ### Install with pipcite33†¶ L63: \nL64: Use the following command to check the version of CUDA and PyTorch\nL65: \nL66:     python -c 'import torch;print(torch.__version__);print(torch.version.cuda)'\nL67: \nL68: \nL69: Select the appropriate installation command depending on the type of system, CUDA version, PyTorch version, and MMCV version\nL70: \nL71: [Select] [Select] [Select] [Select]\nL72: If you do not find a corresponding version in the dropdown box above, you probably do not have a pre-built package corresponding to the PyTorch or CUDA or mmcv version, at which point you can cite31†build mmcv from source .\nL73: \nL74: Note\nL75: mmcv is only compiled on PyTorch 1.x.0 because the compatibility usually holds between 1.x.0 and 1.x.1. If your PyTorch version is 1.x.1, you can install mmcv compiled with PyTorch 1.x.0 and it usually works well. For example, if your PyTorch version is 1.8.1, you can feel free to choose 1.8.x.\nL76: \nL77: Note\nL78: If you would like to use `opencv-python-headless` instead of `opencv-python`, e.g., in a minimum container environment or servers without GUI, you can first install it before installing MMCV to skip the installation of `opencv-python`.\nL79: \nL80: Alternatively, if it takes too long to install a dependency library, you can specify the pypi source\nL81: \nL82:     mim install mmcv -i https://pypi.tuna.tsinghua.edu.cn/simple\nL83: You can run cite32†check_installation.py†github.com to check the installation of mmcv after running the installation commands.\nL84: ### Using mmcv with Dockercite34†¶ L85: \nL86: Build with local repository\nL87: \nL88:     git clone https://github.com/open-mmlab/mmcv.git && cd mmcv\nL89:     docker build -t mmcv -f docker/release/Dockerfile .\nL90: \nL91: \nL92: Or build with remote repository\nL93: \nL94:     docker build -t mmcv https://github.com/open-mmlab/mmcv.git#main:docker/release\nL95: The Dockerfile installs latest released version of mmcv-full by default, but you can specify mmcv versions to install expected versions.\nL96: \nL97:     docker image build -t mmcv -f docker/release/Dockerfile --build-arg MMCV=2.0.0 .\nL98: \nL99: \nL100: If you also want to use other versions of PyTorch and CUDA, you can also pass them when building docker images.\nL101: An example to build an image with PyTorch 1.11 and CUDA 11.3.\nL102: \nL103:     docker build -t mmcv -f docker/release/Dockerfile \\\nL104:         --build-arg PYTORCH=1.11.0 \\\nL105:         --build-arg CUDA=11.3 \\\nL106:         --build-arg CUDNN=8 \\\nL107:         --build-arg MMCV=2.0.0 .\nL108: \nL109: \nL110: More available versions of PyTorch and CUDA can be found at cite35†dockerhub/pytorch†hub.docker.com .\nL111: ## Install mmcv-litecite36†¶ L112: \nL113: If you need to use PyTorch-related modules, make sure PyTorch has been successfully installed in your environment by referring to the cite37†PyTorch official installation guide†github.com .\nL114: \nL115:     pip install mmcv-lite\nL116: \nL117: \nL118: * * *\nL119: \nL120: Built with cite38†Sphinx†sphinx-doc.org using a cite39†theme†github.com provided by cite40†Read the Docs†readthedocs.org .\nL121:   * cite41†Installation L122:     * cite27†Install mmcv L123:       * cite29†Install with mim (recommended) L124:       * cite33†Install with pip L125:       * cite34†Using mmcv with Docker L126:     * cite36†Install mmcv-lite L127: \nL128:   * cite0†GitHub†github.com --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn239view3 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://download.openmmlab.com/mmcv/dist/cu118/torch2.1/index.html\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: URL https://download.openmmlab.com/mmcv/dist/cu118/torch2.1/index.html is not accessible via this tool.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAccurate segmentation of green fruit based on optimized mask RCNN application in complex orchard - PMC (https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9399748/)\nciteturn239view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9399748/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 573\nL0: cite0†Skip to main content L1: \nL2: cite1†Image†cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov Search\nL3: \nL4: cite2†Image†cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov Log in cite3†Image†cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov cite4†Image†cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov L5: \nL6:   * cite5†Dashboard†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov L7:   * cite6†Publications†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov L8:   * cite7†Account settings†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov L9:   * [Button: Log out ]\nL10: \nL11: Search… [Input: Search NCBI] Search NC